lassify.py:215-219 returns NOOP ('Jira already terminal; steady state') BEFORE any target comparison","AC line 2: a project override archived = 'Cancelled' yields target 'Cancelled', which is itself in _JIRA_TERMINAL_STATUSES"],"finding":"The plan restructures the classify() TERMINAL+PRESENT branch but does not state how the new RETIRE_TERMINAL path interacts with the pre-existing early NOOP return that fires when the Jira status is already in _JIRA_TERMINAL_STATUSES (classify.py:215-220). If that NOOP guard is left as a separate earlier return, a bound terminal ticket whose Jira issue is already at a terminal status OTHER than the resolved target (e.g. target 'Done' but issue 'Cancelled', or an override target 'Cancelled') would NOOP forever and its binding would never be retired.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f36a6ea8231cf8a34","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 (Classify) / src/rebar/reconciler/classify.py:211-225","norm_id":"n9a56172c77c8435d","priority":0.625,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A human cancels a bound issue whose resolved terminal target is 'Done'; the binding is expected to retire but the old NOOP branch strands it","An override sets archived = 'Cancelled' and the issue is already Done"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 2, specify that for a TERMINAL local with Jira PRESENT the single new branch is: if terminal_target is None OR jira_status == target OR jira_status in _JIRA_TERMINAL_STATUSES → RETIRE_TERMINAL; else TERMINAL_TRANSITION — and that the former NOOP-on-already-terminal early return is removed, not retained.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify what happens when the terminal transition is rejected/ignored by the Jira workflow (so the issue never reaches the target status): surface the stuck transition (log/metric) and/or bound the repeated outbound emission, so a binding cannot silently re-close forever.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Confirmation is level-triggered: a pass that closes the issue leaves the binding, and the next pass that observes the target (or another terminal) status retires it.'","Observation: the reported defect is exactly a binding that 're-closes it every pass'; a stuck transition reproduces this.","No AC or step covers a transition the Jira workflow refuses, nor a metric/log for bindings that stay un-retired across many passes."],"finding":"The level-triggered confirmation assumes the Jira issue will reach the terminal target status, but gives no handling or observability for a transition that Jira rejects (e.g. a workflow that forbids To Do -> Done directly). In that case the binding is never retired and TERMINAL_TRANSITION re-emits the outbound update every pass — a degraded recurrence of the reported bug.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdf8daeb3050b518d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 (Binding walk) / Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n3fe883d4e59e699e","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Jira project workflow has no direct To Do -> Done path; the outbound {status: Done} is a no-op or error and the issue never reaches a terminal status.","Binding loops forever emitting the same outbound update with no operator visibility."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a step and AC covering transition-failure: if the applier reports the transition failed or the issue does not reach any terminal status after N passes, log/alert the stuck binding rather than silently re-emitting; confirm the breaker or a backoff limits repeated emission.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"find